00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:52.700
So let's dig a
little deeper and see

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:57.060
the building blocks of a
great messaging application.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.430
First and foremost,
you would obviously

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:04.600
need an infinitely and
insanely scalable load balancer

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:07.080
to take the traffic from
millions of users which

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.580
connect to your application.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:15.120
And then you have to connect the
users to the backend systems.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.670
So you need a
mechanism or a system

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:20.500
to manage these
connections efficiently.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.510
And that's where the connection
handling comes into place.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:27.170
And then you need to be able to
authenticate the users you're

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:31.090
connecting to and be able to
deliver these messages securely

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:34.790
and consistently.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:37.410
And obviously, you know, with
so many billions of messages

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:40.420
coming through, you need
a job management system

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.510
which basically
manages these jobs

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:45.570
in an asynchronous fashion.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.740
And then, we have a
message processor.

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.220
A message processor,
basically what

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:52.520
it does is it takes a
message and understand what

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:55.220
needs to be done with that
message, the action that you

00:03:55.220 --> 00:04:00.200
need to take for a single
one-to-one chat or a group chat

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:03.590
or for example, when a user
is online or user is offline,

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.910
the action that it has
to take is different.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:07.880
So the message
processor is the one

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:11.700
which decides what needs to
be done around a message.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:14.880
And obviously, you
need a message store.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.980
Think of it as a
place or a database

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:20.227
where you store all those
billions of messages

00:04:20.227 --> 00:04:22.560
and be able to retrieve those
messages very quickly when

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:24.280
you need them.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:27.940
So you need a database
which can do this for you.

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:33.630
And then, you need a file
store or an object store

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:37.740
to save all those cute cat
videos, the memes that you

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:40.380
share, and the selfies that
you share with your friends.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:45.350
So all these object files go and
get stored in the file storage

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:47.780
as such.

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:50.870
And then notification
management.

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:52.050
This is very key.

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:54.740
So the notification management
system, what it basically does,

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:59.630
it identifies whether the
user is online or offline.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:02.070
And if he's offline, send
him a message saying,

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.660
hey, you've got a
message and bring him

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:07.030
back to the application
to check his messages.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:11.730
So all this is dealt by the
notification management system.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:16.520
Now last but not the least, you
need a great analytics platform

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:18.980
behind this to take
driven decisions

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:22.400
and be able to be agile
in terms of decisions

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:25.380
to ensure the startup
works really well.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:30.440
So to see now that you know all
the basic building blocks here,

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:33.260
we're going to see how these
things are put together.

